@description ReaVim: vim mode for REAPER (extension)
@author Perken
@version 0.3.0
@provides
  [linux64] reaper_reavim.so https://github.com/AntoineBalaine/perken-reaper-scripts/releases/download/reavim-ext-v$version/reaper_reavim-linux-x86_64.so
  [linux-aarch64] reaper_reavim.so https://github.com/AntoineBalaine/perken-reaper-scripts/releases/download/reavim-ext-v$version/reaper_reavim-linux-aarch64.so
  [darwin64] reaper_reavim.dylib https://github.com/AntoineBalaine/perken-reaper-scripts/releases/download/reavim-ext-v$version/reaper_reavim-macos-x86_64.dylib
  [darwin-arm64] reaper_reavim.dylib https://github.com/AntoineBalaine/perken-reaper-scripts/releases/download/reavim-ext-v$version/reaper_reavim-macos-aarch64.dylib
  [win64] reaper_reavim.dll https://github.com/AntoineBalaine/perken-reaper-scripts/releases/download/reavim-ext-v$version/reaper_reavim-windows-x86_64.dll
@changelog
  First release as a ReaPack package.
@link
  Source repository https://github.com/AntoineBalaine/perken-reaper-scripts
@about
  # ReaVim extension

  The compiled successor of the ReaVim Lua scripts. It does not replace your keymap.
  Default bindings are built in; copy bindings.ini from the GitHub release to Data/Perken to edit them.
